#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - Makefile version-header generation breaks when
# building from a source tarball without .git (git describe + \# escape)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libfirm-1.22.0-makefile-version-header-tarball
trigger_tool:           make|git
phase:                  build
error_signature:        "expected identifier or '\\('.*firm_revision|git describe.*fatal.*not a git repository|\\#define libfirm_VERSION_REVISION"
severity:               1
category:               build-system, make, portability, build-tool
match_keywords:         git describe, version header, firm_revision.h, tarball, no .git, make, shell escape, libfirm
title:                  Makefile version-header via `git describe` breaks on tarball builds (no .git): provide fallback REVISION and avoid `\#` escaping

root_cause:             Upstream Makefiles often synthesize a version header from
                        `git describe`. When building from a release tarball
                        (no .git directory) git describe fails, REVISION is empty,
                        and the generated header becomes invalid C. In libfirm the
                        header line was emitted via `REV="\#define ..."` — the
                        backslash before # is preserved by the shell inside double
                        quotes, producing a literal `\#define` line which the C
                        preprocessor rejects ("expected identifier or '('").

rec_approach:           In the Makefile:
                        1) make git describe non-fatal with a fallback revision:
                           `git ... describe ... 2>/dev/null || echo <tag-hash>`;
                        2) emit the #define without a shell-escaping backslash,
                           e.g. `printf '\x23define ...'` or plain "#define ...".

verification_cmd:       cat build/gen/firm_revision.h
verification:           Before: `\#define libfirm_VERSION_REVISION ""` → C error.
                        After: `#define libfirm_VERSION_REVISION "2259fe47..."` and
                        `make` exit 0. Verified in libfirm 1.22.0 tarball build.

affected_scope:         Autotools/Make projects generating a version header from
                        git describe, when built from tarball sources (conan get,
                        CI) instead of a git checkout.

forbid_1_pattern:       rm.*firm_revision|commit.*generated header
forbid_1_reason:        The header is a build artifact; removing it or committing it
                        masks the make-logic bug and pollutes the PR.
forbid_1_consequence:   Unreproducible builds / junk in the archive diff.

similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

